MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 906380680}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 1503127169, guid: af56af93b18e8464f9915f7a446a8088, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Notes: '## Physics Setup


    The sample uses a script to make temporary changes
    to project physics settings while playing. Normally you would set these in your
    project, but we don''t want to change project settings for a sample scene.


    The
    sample also uses the Water layer for enemies, to avoid adding layers to your
    project. But again, normally you would add an Enemy layer.'
